# wacuum.voltrevo.com: TLS and HTTP/2 from Caddy, everything else from the devnet on loopback.
#
# Caddy writes the client's address into X-Forwarded-For (replacing whatever the client sent, since no
# proxy in front of it is trusted), and the devnet takes the last entry of that header as the visitor the
# faucet limits. So the devnet must listen on loopback only, which is its default.
#
# The devnet can answer only a few dozen connections at once (src/server.wac says why), so Caddy does the
# waiting for slow clients: it reads every request whole, headers and body, before it passes it on, and gives
# up on a client that takes more than ten seconds to send one. Nothing the devnet answers needs more than a
# megabyte.
{
	servers {
		timeouts {
			read_header 10s
			read_body 10s
		}
	}
}

wacuum.voltrevo.com {
	encode zstd gzip
	request_body {
		max_size 1MB
	}
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8545 {
		request_buffers 1MB
	}
}
